<section class="home-section about-section">
	<p class="home-eyebrow">A little about me</p>
	<h2>About me</h2>
	<p>I grew up on a farm in Lancashire, in the North of England, surrounded by more fields and livestock than computers and technology. 
        Growing up outside a major city meant that I had considerably less exposure to technology and the internet than many people my age. 
        Despite this, I developed a strong interest in Computer Science and found that I particularly enjoyed the process of breaking down difficult 
        problems and finding simple, elegant solutions to them. That interest eventually led me to study Computer Science at the University of Oxford.
        <br><br>
        My biggest area of interest is in playing games, I have always been a competitive person, having played Tennis from a young age and loving competing 
        against others. An aspiration of mine is to be able to conduct research into this field and develop algorithms capable of finding optimal or near optimal 
        strategies in games. Machine Learning, and especially Reinforcement Learning is my favourite topic, due to the fact that an agent can develop strategies 
        through experience rather than being explicitly taught how to solve a problem. Watching models discover tactics in games such as Chess that a human may 
        never have thought of is extraordinary. Zero-sum games are especially intriguing to me due to the agents' objectives being directly opposed: a gain 
        in reward for one agent corresponds to a loss for another. This naturally connects Reinforcement Learning with areas such as game theory and probabilistic 
        decision-making, which are areas I am keen to explore further.
        <br><br>
        Outside of academia, I enjoy time with family, which includes 2 cats which I absolutely adore, play Tennis and video games with friends and just relax. 
        Most importantly, I love what I do.
    </p>
